My first post to rgrn was 'few questions (primarily dealing with
Amulet of Yendor)' on 4/17 (yesterday, well actually 1am this
morning).  I included a little background in that post, but I'll
repost it here.

I have never ascended a character before now.  I usually got bored
after a certain point (when I felt my character was practically
invincible) and I stopped playing the game at that time.  So, in order
to challenge myself, I'm went for a vegan, athiest, illiterate,
genoless, polypileless, polyselfless, wishless, and boneless
ascension.  'Boneless' means that I deleted any bones files before
starting a new game-- this makes it much harder for the next character
since he doesn't get the benefit of getting any decent items quickly
(especially magic resistance).  I've tried several times over the past
couple of months, but the darn polymorph traps kept getting me and I
very rarely had magic resistance or even just polymorph control.

My race and class of choice was a dwarven Valkyrie.  I didn't keep any
notes, so this post is a recollection of the events that occurred
within the last week.  I ran around the main dungeon for a while until
I reached xlvl 5.  Then, I dipped for Excalibur and went back through
the mines to Gnome Town.  Found a bag of holding and bought a magic
whistle.  Went to Sokoban, retrieved amulet of reflection.  Found a
ring of polymorph control as well.  Went back to Gnomish mines and
obtained the luckstone.  Fiddled around the dungeon, cleaning out
levels (including several throne rooms, one of whose thrones allowed
me to identify all items in my visible inventory, which later was
erased by several (master) mind flayers).  Found a polymorph trap and
tried to zap a wand of create monster and lure the monsters into the
trap, hoping to get a gray dragon.  Got one, killed it, no scales :(. 
Revived it several times, killed it several times, no scales :(.  Went
back to level 1, kicked a sink, got a inccubus and did the dance (for
quite a while since my charisma was only 9).  Finally, I reached xlvl
14, did the Quest and retrieved the Orb of Fate.  Hit a polymorph trap
and went back down to xlvl 12 (oh well).  Went down to the Castle and
went around the back door.  Found a gray dragon.  Killed it, revived
it several times, but no scales :(.  Encountered 1st lich who quickly
destroyed my speed boots (it would be a while before I'd get a new
pair in hell).  Cleared out the rest of the castle and went back,
hoping for Ludious.  Found it.  Found gray dragon, killed it, got
scales.  Woohoo!  At last, magic resistance.  Went down through hell,
killed everything and left top level of Wizard tower undone.  Went
back to castle level (this was my home base) and fixed up my ascension
kit.  Went back down, killed Rodney, got the Book of the Dead.  Went
to Moloch's Sanctum, got the Amulet and made a dash for level 1. 
Along the way, I didn't expect to keep getting malignant aura messages
and random monsters popping up due to the Amulet being in my
possession, but it was no problem.  As an aside, up to now, I only had
one really close call: I thought cancellation would remove a master
mind flayer's "brain-sucking" attack, and when I walked up to it to
bash it, it still sucked me down to exactly Int 3 (wasn't paying
attention).  Luckily/"Intelligently", I had a wand of death in my
visible inventory and zap the MMF to oblivion.  Anyway, back to the
ascension story.  I went up to Earth, used the Orb of Fate to find the
portal and dug directly to the portal via wands of digging.  Went to
air, put on levitation ring and found portal via search.  Went to fire
and a monster conveniently "disappeared" into the magic portal and so
I just went directly there.  Went to water and floated around a bit
until I found the portal via searching.  Went to Astral.  Encountered
Pestilence.  Used ring of conflict and a nice Olog-Hai killed it for
me.  Went to the left.  Darn-- neutral altar.  As I was going back, I
got stuck next to Pestilence.  I zapped my wand of death-- missed. 
Uh, oh.  I zapped my last charge-- hit it.  Whew.  Went to middle one
next and encountered Famine.  Used magic harp to tame Olog-hai,
displaced his position, and asked it nicely to kill Famine (twice). 
Then, I went directly to altar and found it to be lawful.  Sacrified
the amulet and sighed a breath of relief.

